WEBVTT

00:00:04.781 --> 00:00:05.521
Hi.

00:00:05.781 --> 00:00:08.022
Welcome to Steadfast Men.

00:00:08.302 --> 00:00:10.242
This is Lesson One.

00:00:10.482 --> 00:00:14.003
Today's lesson is called A Quiet Tuesday.

00:00:14.263 --> 00:00:16.504
Here's what you and I are going to cover.

00:00:16.824 --> 00:00:23.685
First, what I mean by a Tuesday,
and why God builds a man on the plain days.

00:00:24.126 --> 00:00:28.927
Second, why being busy isn't
the same as being there.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:33.108
Third, the first mark of a steadfast man.

00:00:33.248 --> 00:00:35.648
It's called Stop Waiting.

00:00:35.948 --> 00:00:40.710
Then the reasons you might
give me for waiting, I'm Wes.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:41.930
Wes Hart.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.471
I'm a husband. I'm a dad.

00:00:44.651 --> 00:00:47.932
I've got a job I go to
every day, same as you.

00:00:48.172 --> 00:00:52.073
And for the next twenty-four lessons,
I'm going to be your teacher.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.013
I don't know where you are right now.

00:00:55.194 --> 00:00:59.174
Maybe the kids are finally asleep
and you've got the laptop open.

00:00:59.435 --> 00:01:01.135
Maybe you're in your truck on a lunch

00:01:01.175 --> 00:01:03.495
break with your phone
propped on the wheel.

00:01:03.756 --> 00:01:07.336
Maybe a buddy sent you the link
and you're giving it five minutes.

00:01:07.596 --> 00:01:10.957
Wherever you are,
I'm glad you clicked on this.

00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:12.137
I mean that.

00:01:12.258 --> 00:01:13.878
And I'd bet on something.

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:17.179
You told somebody, or maybe just yourself,

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:20.879
that you were only going to
check this out. Just looking.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.220
No promises.

00:01:23.147 --> 00:01:24.227
That's fine.

00:01:24.487 --> 00:01:26.308
I started out that way too.

00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:27.808
I'm still here.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:32.309
So before you get going,
I want you to hear one thing from me.

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:34.550
You're on time.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.431
Maybe you're young,
and you're still waiting

00:01:37.471 --> 00:01:40.191
for somebody to tell you you're a man.

00:01:40.551 --> 00:01:42.232
You're on time.

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:46.753
Maybe you're married and your kids
are climbing all over you every night.

00:01:46.993 --> 00:01:48.673
You're on time.

00:01:49.073 --> 00:01:54.275
Maybe you're divorced, you're still a dad,
and the house got real quiet.

00:01:54.575 --> 00:01:56.255
You're on time.

00:01:56.675 --> 00:01:59.436
Maybe you figured this
was for somebody younger.

00:01:59.856 --> 00:02:01.476
You're on time.

00:02:01.696 --> 00:02:03.277
You're not a guest here.

00:02:03.377 --> 00:02:04.797
This is yours.

00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:07.738
So here's what I'll promise you.

00:02:08.098 --> 00:02:09.918
I won't waste your time.

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:11.739
I'm not going to yell at you.

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:14.960
And I'm not going to tell you
everything's fine, either.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.640
I'm going to teach you something true.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.921
I'll show you where it
shows up in a normal day.

00:02:21.181 --> 00:02:24.042
Then I'll give you one thing to go do.

00:02:24.882 --> 00:02:25.582
Okay.

00:02:25.762 --> 00:02:27.243
Here's how this goes.

00:02:27.563 --> 00:02:32.104
You and I do this one lesson at a time.
Twenty-four of them.

00:02:32.306 --> 00:02:37.207
Every lesson is built the same way,
so you'll always know where you are.

00:02:37.447 --> 00:02:39.307
First, I teach.

00:02:39.468 --> 00:02:40.768
That's this part.

00:02:41.555 --> 00:02:44.896
Have your Bible open and
your workbook next to you.

00:02:45.076 --> 00:02:49.217
If you don't have the workbook yet,
a notebook and a pen are fine.

00:02:49.597 --> 00:02:52.517
Second, you stop and think.

00:02:52.837 --> 00:02:58.038
A few times in every lesson I'll ask you
to pause this and write something down.

00:02:58.179 --> 00:02:59.799
Don't skip those.

00:02:59.919 --> 00:03:02.439
That's where the lesson becomes yours.

00:03:02.719 --> 00:03:06.560
And third, you walk away with one move.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:07.520
One.

00:03:07.661 --> 00:03:08.821
Not a list.

00:03:09.162 --> 00:03:10.362
Why just one?

00:03:10.582 --> 00:03:13.403
Because I've been handed plenty of lists.

00:03:13.523 --> 00:03:14.623
You have too.

00:03:14.923 --> 00:03:17.404
A list feels great on Sunday.

00:03:17.504 --> 00:03:21.605
By Wednesday it's on the floor of
the truck with the fast-food bags.

00:03:22.005 --> 00:03:24.345
One move you can actually do.

00:03:24.725 --> 00:03:26.586
And at the start of the next lesson,

00:03:26.626 --> 00:03:29.486
the first thing I'll
ask you is how it went.

00:03:29.666 --> 00:03:33.427
If you've got a friend doing this with you,
he's going to ask you too.

00:03:33.787 --> 00:03:34.567
Let him.

00:03:34.688 --> 00:03:36.288
That's the whole plan.

00:03:36.528 --> 00:03:40.049
Show up. Tell the truth. Do the move.

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:43.669
So get a pen. Turn your phone face down.

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:45.130
Let's get to work.

00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:49.177
Here's the big idea of this lesson.

00:03:49.317 --> 00:03:53.218
If you only remember one sentence,
make it this one.

00:03:53.478 --> 00:03:58.058
A man's life gets decided on
the days nobody photographs.

00:03:59.498 --> 00:04:00.879
Say that to yourself.

00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:04.079
The days nobody photographs.

00:04:04.519 --> 00:04:07.399
Think about the days
that do get photographed.

00:04:07.559 --> 00:04:08.539
Your wedding.

00:04:08.639 --> 00:04:09.559
A baby.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:10.840
A new job.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.040
Those days are real. God uses them.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:16.361
I've got nothing against a big day.

00:04:16.581 --> 00:04:18.161
But let me ask you something.

00:04:18.341 --> 00:04:22.341
Have you ever had one of those days
you were sure would change you?

00:04:22.621 --> 00:04:26.262
A vow you meant.
A night in a hospital hallway.

00:04:26.422 --> 00:04:29.682
A Sunday you walked out
of church a different man.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.122
Be honest with me.

00:04:31.342 --> 00:04:35.883
Did the next ordinary day look a
lot like the ordinary day before it?

00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:38.623
Yeah. Mine too.

00:04:39.043 --> 00:04:42.984
A big day can mark you.
It can't give you a habit.

00:04:43.204 --> 00:04:46.504
A habit is what a lot of
plain days leave on you.

00:04:46.684 --> 00:04:48.684
And most of your days aren't big.

00:04:48.784 --> 00:04:51.064
Most of them are just Tuesday.

00:04:51.444 --> 00:04:53.025
Jesus put it this way.

00:04:53.205 --> 00:04:55.865
Luke chapter sixteen, verse ten.

00:04:56.712 --> 00:05:01.793
"Whoever can be trusted with very
little can also be trusted with much,

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:07.135
and whoever is dishonest with very
little will also be dishonest with much."

00:05:08.336 --> 00:05:12.077
Let's slow down and actually read that.
Look at it with me.

00:05:12.437 --> 00:05:14.957
Jesus is talking about a manager.

00:05:15.058 --> 00:05:17.858
A man who's in charge of
somebody else's money.

00:05:18.138 --> 00:05:19.839
And look at what He measures.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.800
Not the big account. The small one.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.081
Two words show up twice in that verse.
Did you catch them?

00:05:27.421 --> 00:05:28.762
Very little.

00:05:29.022 --> 00:05:30.642
That's Tuesday talk.

00:05:30.922 --> 00:05:34.003
Very little is the tone
you use when you're tired.

00:05:34.063 --> 00:05:36.004
It's a text you owe somebody.

00:05:36.144 --> 00:05:38.044
It's ten minutes with your kid.

00:05:38.265 --> 00:05:40.405
And the verse cuts both ways.

00:05:40.605 --> 00:05:43.586
Trusted in little, trusted in much.

00:05:43.806 --> 00:05:47.127
Dishonest in little, dishonest in much.

00:05:47.327 --> 00:05:49.948
The small stuff doesn't stay small.

00:05:50.048 --> 00:05:52.709
It shows up again when
the stakes get bigger.

00:05:52.949 --> 00:05:54.189
So let me ask you.

00:05:54.389 --> 00:05:57.610
Where does God build a man?
On the big day?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.111
Or on the plain one?

00:05:59.251 --> 00:06:02.092
The plain one. The very little.

00:06:02.252 --> 00:06:04.933
That's this whole lesson in two words.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:07.300
Okay.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.000
Here's the first point.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.281
What do I mean when I say a Tuesday?

00:06:12.761 --> 00:06:16.421
I mean a day with nothing
on it worth dressing up for.

00:06:16.681 --> 00:06:18.362
You come home tired.

00:06:18.582 --> 00:06:20.822
Or you never left the apartment.

00:06:20.902 --> 00:06:24.082
And the loudest thing in
the house is your phone.

00:06:24.262 --> 00:06:27.523
And right in front of
you there's a small yes.

00:06:27.843 --> 00:06:29.243
Something you could say.

00:06:29.483 --> 00:06:30.603
Or swallow.

00:06:31.083 --> 00:06:32.983
I call it a Tuesday.

00:06:33.203 --> 00:06:36.584
If your hard day is Thursday,
call it Thursday.

00:06:36.724 --> 00:06:40.004
The name doesn't matter. The day does.

00:06:40.384 --> 00:06:43.045
I'll tell you how I dodge my Tuesdays.

00:06:43.165 --> 00:06:44.805
I'm really good at it.

00:06:45.045 --> 00:06:49.246
I've prayed out loud, "God,
make me a better man."

00:06:49.506 --> 00:06:54.006
Then I spent the next half hour on
my phone comparing leaf blowers.

00:06:54.286 --> 00:06:55.486
Thirty minutes.

00:06:55.606 --> 00:06:58.267
Reviews. Decibel ratings.

00:06:58.407 --> 00:07:01.987
The prayer was real.
The phone was just easier.

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:04.568
I'd guess you're a little like that too.

00:07:04.708 --> 00:07:07.188
You'll research a tool for an hour.

00:07:07.268 --> 00:07:10.168
You won't look at your
own day for five minutes.

00:07:10.968 --> 00:07:13.449
Let me tell you about one of my Tuesdays,

00:07:13.489 --> 00:07:15.869
so you know I'm not talking down to you.

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:17.909
My daughter had a bike.

00:07:17.989 --> 00:07:22.330
The back tire had been soft for
a couple of days. Maybe four.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:27.451
One afternoon she met me at the
door and said, "Dad, can we fix it?

00:07:27.511 --> 00:07:28.371
Together?"

00:07:28.751 --> 00:07:31.651
It wasn't a crisis. It was a tire.

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.911
I said, "After supper."

00:07:34.111 --> 00:07:35.292
And I meant it.

00:07:35.472 --> 00:07:38.172
Right then, I was a good dad.

00:07:38.452 --> 00:07:39.392
We ate.

00:07:39.552 --> 00:07:42.533
Then I opened my laptop,
because there was one

00:07:42.573 --> 00:07:45.793
thing I didn't want hanging
over me in the morning.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:47.840
One thing.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:50.060
That's what I told myself.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:52.841
It turned into the next thing.

00:07:53.361 --> 00:07:55.561
I could hear her in the other room.

00:07:55.921 --> 00:07:58.341
At some point she rolled
the bike out to the

00:07:58.381 --> 00:08:01.501
edge of the patio and
went back to her homework.

00:08:01.902 --> 00:08:03.422
I didn't see her do it.

00:08:04.002 --> 00:08:07.902
Late that night I let the dog out.
Porch light on.

00:08:08.182 --> 00:08:09.582
And there's the bike.

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:11.562
Tire still soft.

00:08:11.942 --> 00:08:14.043
The pump was in the hall closet,

00:08:14.083 --> 00:08:17.023
right where I'd pictured the
two of us getting it out.

00:08:17.343 --> 00:08:19.083
So I fixed it.

00:08:19.303 --> 00:08:20.343
In the dark.

00:08:20.483 --> 00:08:21.743
By myself.

00:08:22.123 --> 00:08:23.864
And I felt useful.

00:08:24.184 --> 00:08:28.424
That's a dangerous feeling for
a man who just missed the point.

00:08:29.004 --> 00:08:32.805
The next morning she saw
the tire and said, "Oh.

00:08:32.985 --> 00:08:33.825
Thanks."

00:08:34.305 --> 00:08:35.825
That was all she said.

00:08:36.125 --> 00:08:38.385
She'd already stopped waiting on me.

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.545
I did the job.

00:08:40.785 --> 00:08:42.465
And I missed my girl.

00:08:43.646 --> 00:08:45.826
Let's stop right here for a minute.

00:08:46.006 --> 00:08:49.466
Think about yesterday. Just yesterday.

00:08:49.686 --> 00:08:53.807
Find one small yes that
was right in front of you.

00:08:53.947 --> 00:08:55.007
A person.

00:08:55.107 --> 00:08:56.407
Not a task.

00:08:56.607 --> 00:08:57.747
Did you say it?

00:08:57.907 --> 00:08:59.447
Or did you swallow it?

00:09:00.547 --> 00:09:03.047
Open your workbook to Lesson One.

00:09:03.188 --> 00:09:07.808
In the margin, write one word
for where you went instead.

00:09:08.068 --> 00:09:08.968
Phone.

00:09:09.208 --> 00:09:09.968
Work.

00:09:10.228 --> 00:09:10.988
Later.

00:09:11.128 --> 00:09:13.629
Tired. Whatever's true.

00:09:13.809 --> 00:09:17.989
Nobody else has to see it.
Just be honest with the page.

00:09:18.169 --> 00:09:20.149
Pause this and write it.

00:09:22.229 --> 00:09:23.029
Got it?

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:27.030
Good. Hang on to that word.
I'm coming back to it.

00:09:28.657 --> 00:09:31.898
Here's the second point,
and this one's sneaky.

00:09:32.418 --> 00:09:35.498
That night with the bike, I wasn't lazy.

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:36.979
I was busy.

00:09:37.479 --> 00:09:39.939
And busy will lie to you.

00:09:40.259 --> 00:09:42.020
The lie goes like this.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:45.560
"I was busy, so I must have been there."

00:09:46.021 --> 00:09:47.421
I wasn't there.

00:09:47.841 --> 00:09:51.482
Busy is an easy place
for a good man to hide.

00:09:51.622 --> 00:09:54.642
He's competent, so nobody looks closer.

00:09:54.943 --> 00:09:58.783
If you're getting things done,
nobody asks questions.

00:09:59.003 --> 00:10:00.344
Least of all you.

00:10:00.924 --> 00:10:02.164
Here's another one.

00:10:02.304 --> 00:10:04.024
This one's about my wife.

00:10:04.465 --> 00:10:07.045
A while back I owed her an apology.

00:10:07.485 --> 00:10:08.685
One sentence.

00:10:09.027 --> 00:10:11.987
I practiced it at a red
light on the way home.

00:10:12.227 --> 00:10:14.288
I had the true sentence ready.

00:10:14.508 --> 00:10:16.768
The one that would cost me something.

00:10:17.088 --> 00:10:21.209
And I had a softer one behind it,
in case I lost my nerve.

00:10:21.509 --> 00:10:25.750
By the time I pulled into the driveway,
the true one was gone.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:28.991
I walked in and said, "Long day."

00:10:29.491 --> 00:10:31.171
She got a weather report.

00:10:31.391 --> 00:10:33.352
I got to feel like I'd shown up.

00:10:33.572 --> 00:10:35.312
We were three feet apart,

00:10:35.352 --> 00:10:39.213
and I was finishing a conversation
she was never part of.

00:10:40.033 --> 00:10:45.654
Years ago an older man I trusted asked
me a question I still don't enjoy.

00:10:45.975 --> 00:10:48.055
He'd earned the right to ask it.

00:10:48.802 --> 00:10:51.543
He said, "What did you
do yesterday that the

00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:54.263
people in your house
couldn't have hired out?"

00:10:54.663 --> 00:10:56.124
I had my answer ready.

00:10:56.404 --> 00:10:57.904
I'd worked a full day.

00:10:58.044 --> 00:11:02.185
I'd fixed a dripping faucet.
I'd cleared out a pile of messages.

00:11:02.425 --> 00:11:05.786
I handed him that list the
way a boy turns in homework.

00:11:06.146 --> 00:11:07.166
He nodded.

00:11:07.367 --> 00:11:08.287
Patient.

00:11:08.427 --> 00:11:09.727
Almost kind.

00:11:10.007 --> 00:11:13.508
And then he said,
"I didn't ask what you finished.

00:11:13.708 --> 00:11:15.648
I asked where you were."

00:11:16.869 --> 00:11:19.149
That question still stops me.

00:11:19.489 --> 00:11:24.231
You can be the hero of your to-do
list and a stranger in your own house.

00:11:24.351 --> 00:11:27.511
And if you live alone,
nobody's there to push back.

00:11:27.611 --> 00:11:29.692
It's easy to let yourself off.

00:11:30.252 --> 00:11:32.673
So is this about doing less?

00:11:33.073 --> 00:11:33.573
No.

00:11:33.873 --> 00:11:37.514
The tire needed air.
The faucet needed fixing.

00:11:37.634 --> 00:11:39.134
Work is good.

00:11:39.294 --> 00:11:43.435
It's about where you are
while you do it. Not how much.

00:11:43.575 --> 00:11:44.375
Where.

00:11:45.576 --> 00:11:47.956
Let's put together what we've got so far.

00:11:48.377 --> 00:11:49.037
One.

00:11:49.277 --> 00:11:53.478
A man's life gets decided on
the days nobody photographs.

00:11:53.738 --> 00:11:54.418
Two.

00:11:54.818 --> 00:11:57.339
God builds you in the very little.

00:11:57.619 --> 00:11:58.359
Three.

00:11:58.759 --> 00:12:01.400
Busy is not the same as there.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.740
If any of that's fuzzy,
go back and catch it again.

00:12:04.861 --> 00:12:05.581
I'll wait.

00:12:05.721 --> 00:12:06.901
I'm good at waiting.

00:12:07.081 --> 00:12:09.742
And that's exactly the problem.

00:12:11.349 --> 00:12:12.889
Here's the third point.

00:12:12.989 --> 00:12:14.890
And this one has a name.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:19.511
Over these lessons you'll learn
four marks of a steadfast man.

00:12:19.631 --> 00:12:21.791
Today you get the first one.

00:12:22.091 --> 00:12:23.652
Stop Waiting.

00:12:23.852 --> 00:12:28.573
Here's the verse that goes with it.
James chapter four, verse seventeen.

00:12:28.973 --> 00:12:31.694
"If anyone, then,
knows the good they ought

00:12:31.734 --> 00:12:35.454
to do and doesn't do it,
it is sin for them."

00:12:36.675 --> 00:12:38.195
Read that one slowly.

00:12:38.415 --> 00:12:41.336
It doesn't say, does something terrible.

00:12:41.376 --> 00:12:45.417
It says, knows the good,
and doesn't do it.

00:12:45.617 --> 00:12:46.857
That's waiting.

00:12:47.037 --> 00:12:49.998
You know the yes. You just put it off.

00:12:50.238 --> 00:12:52.818
You're probably not refusing to show up.

00:12:52.918 --> 00:12:54.019
You're waiting.

00:12:54.319 --> 00:12:55.459
I know I do it.

00:12:55.659 --> 00:12:57.379
Waiting for a better season.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.000
Waiting to feel ready.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:00.900
Waiting for after supper.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.101
Let me tell you about my twenties.

00:13:03.421 --> 00:13:07.522
I figured manhood would show up one
day like a package on the porch.

00:13:07.762 --> 00:13:10.222
Some morning I'd wake up, the hesitation

00:13:10.262 --> 00:13:13.183
would be gone, and real life would start.

00:13:13.423 --> 00:13:18.064
The package never came.
The hesitation just got older along with me.

00:13:18.884 --> 00:13:20.405
Paul wrote about this.

00:13:20.525 --> 00:13:23.265
First Corinthians thirteen, verse eleven.

00:13:23.485 --> 00:13:26.426
"When I was a child,
I talked like a child,

00:13:26.466 --> 00:13:29.927
I thought like a child,
I reasoned like a child.

00:13:30.067 --> 00:13:34.248
When I became a man,
I put the ways of childhood behind me."

00:13:35.455 --> 00:13:36.955
Look at the first half.

00:13:37.195 --> 00:13:38.175
Talked.

00:13:38.395 --> 00:13:39.216
Thought.

00:13:39.516 --> 00:13:40.516
Reasoned.

00:13:40.696 --> 00:13:44.636
He doesn't say,
when I was a child I had toys.

00:13:44.977 --> 00:13:47.457
All three of those are on the inside.

00:13:47.597 --> 00:13:49.677
You can have a mortgage, a title,

00:13:49.717 --> 00:13:53.158
and a good name,
and still be thinking like a boy.

00:13:53.498 --> 00:13:55.178
Now look at the second half.

00:13:55.538 --> 00:13:57.218
I put them behind me.

00:13:57.499 --> 00:14:01.299
They didn't fall off on his birthday.
He put them there.

00:14:01.359 --> 00:14:02.639
On purpose.

00:14:02.999 --> 00:14:05.320
A boy's yes is real.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.000
That's what makes it tricky.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.741
It lasts exactly as long
as the feeling behind it.

00:14:10.921 --> 00:14:14.921
A man's yes is still standing
after the feeling's gone.

00:14:15.121 --> 00:14:19.082
Now, stop waiting doesn't
mean stop resting.

00:14:19.142 --> 00:14:21.942
Hear me on that. Rest is good.

00:14:22.042 --> 00:14:25.903
A nap is allowed.
A quiet evening is a gift.

00:14:26.103 --> 00:14:28.103
Waiting is something else.

00:14:28.263 --> 00:14:32.884
Waiting is being gone from what's yours
while you keep busy with something else.

00:14:34.104 --> 00:14:35.104
Pause again.

00:14:35.365 --> 00:14:39.805
What are you waiting on before you start?
A better job? A wife?

00:14:39.885 --> 00:14:41.085
A clearer head?

00:14:41.205 --> 00:14:43.046
Your dad to finally say it?

00:14:43.266 --> 00:14:46.946
Write it under your word.
Just the thing you're waiting on.

00:14:49.067 --> 00:14:49.747
Okay.

00:14:49.827 --> 00:14:54.468
Now look at it and ask yourself,
is that really mine to wait on?

00:14:54.568 --> 00:14:56.168
Or is it mine to start?

00:14:57.755 --> 00:15:00.076
You might already be arguing with me.

00:15:00.256 --> 00:15:01.396
That's good.

00:15:01.536 --> 00:15:04.617
Let's take those one at a time. First one.

00:15:05.017 --> 00:15:07.377
"Wes, I'm just tired."

00:15:07.798 --> 00:15:08.798
I believe you.

00:15:09.018 --> 00:15:11.378
You might be carrying a lot right now.

00:15:11.659 --> 00:15:16.080
A job that takes everything it can.
A house full of need.

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:21.501
If you're barely holding on,
hear this as an invitation, not a whip.

00:15:21.861 --> 00:15:25.402
Some nights,
going to sleep is the faithful thing.

00:15:25.642 --> 00:15:30.743
But if you're just comfortable being gone,
don't borrow the tired man's excuse.

00:15:30.924 --> 00:15:32.984
God knows which one you are.

00:15:33.104 --> 00:15:35.185
And honestly, so do you.

00:15:35.985 --> 00:15:37.025
Second one.

00:15:37.405 --> 00:15:39.686
"Nobody ever showed me how."

00:15:39.986 --> 00:15:43.367
That's true for more fathers
and sons than you'd think.

00:15:43.607 --> 00:15:49.288
Nobody stood next to you on a plain day and said,
here, this is what a man does.

00:15:49.568 --> 00:15:51.249
I'm not blaming you for that.

00:15:51.349 --> 00:15:52.949
But look at the verse again.

00:15:53.069 --> 00:15:57.390
Paul didn't say,
when my father finally did his job.

00:15:57.511 --> 00:16:02.872
He said, when I became a man,
I put the ways of childhood behind me.

00:16:03.132 --> 00:16:06.593
That door's open whether
anybody showed you or not.

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:08.500
Third one.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:10.301
"I'm too old.

00:16:10.481 --> 00:16:13.582
I'm retired. That's for a younger man."

00:16:14.302 --> 00:16:16.523
I know a man I'll call Howard.

00:16:16.663 --> 00:16:17.943
Late sixties.

00:16:18.063 --> 00:16:20.504
Retired, and he earned it.

00:16:20.764 --> 00:16:24.225
His grandson asked him to
come see a project at school.

00:16:24.565 --> 00:16:26.546
Howard said he was tired.

00:16:26.746 --> 00:16:27.726
He was.

00:16:27.986 --> 00:16:29.346
He went anyway.

00:16:29.527 --> 00:16:33.348
And on the ride home,
that boy talked the whole way.

00:16:33.748 --> 00:16:37.889
Howard called me that night and said,
"I thought the job was over.

00:16:37.989 --> 00:16:39.709
The boy didn't get the memo."

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.070
The job might be over.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.231
Being a man didn't clock out with it.

00:16:46.031 --> 00:16:47.152
And one more.

00:16:47.472 --> 00:16:51.913
"I'm single. I live alone.
Who am I even showing up for?"

00:16:52.433 --> 00:16:55.454
Somebody you can reach still needs you.

00:16:55.634 --> 00:16:57.675
A brother. A friend.

00:16:57.795 --> 00:17:00.596
A kid at church who
doesn't have a dad around.

00:17:00.876 --> 00:17:05.177
And God, who's been in that
apartment with you the whole time.

00:17:05.417 --> 00:17:07.458
He's seen your Tuesday already.

00:17:07.738 --> 00:17:10.299
Show up for it where He can see it.

00:17:11.906 --> 00:17:16.707
So what does this look like on a real
Monday morning? Let's get practical.

00:17:16.927 --> 00:17:17.987
You wake up.

00:17:18.228 --> 00:17:21.808
Before you open your phone,
you ask one question.

00:17:22.008 --> 00:17:23.469
Who's mine today?

00:17:23.769 --> 00:17:25.469
Not what's on my list.

00:17:25.589 --> 00:17:26.969
Who's mine.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:30.650
At breakfast, if your kid
starts telling you something,

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.391
you put the cup down and look at your kid.

00:17:33.611 --> 00:17:34.931
Thirty seconds.

00:17:35.271 --> 00:17:38.832
On the drive in, you send the
text you've been putting off.

00:17:38.972 --> 00:17:41.073
The one you know you owe.

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:45.414
At work, you do the job well.
That's part of it too.

00:17:45.674 --> 00:17:47.774
And when you walk in the door that night,

00:17:47.814 --> 00:17:51.875
the true sentence comes
out before "long day" does.

00:17:52.215 --> 00:17:54.856
Nobody's going to photograph any of that.

00:17:55.016 --> 00:17:56.476
All of it counts.

00:17:57.677 --> 00:18:00.857
Okay. So here's your one move.

00:18:01.217 --> 00:18:01.878
One.

00:18:02.018 --> 00:18:05.199
eat one meal with your
phone in another room.

00:18:05.399 --> 00:18:09.039
Not in your pocket.
Not face down next to your plate.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.760
In another room.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:14.241
If you live alone,
you still sit down to eat.

00:18:14.341 --> 00:18:17.001
And the phone still
goes in the other room.

00:18:17.382 --> 00:18:19.042
Then one more piece.

00:18:19.302 --> 00:18:21.542
Text one man you trust.

00:18:21.723 --> 00:18:24.423
Ask him, "What did you
do with your Tuesday?"

00:18:24.663 --> 00:18:26.243
And let him ask you back.

00:18:26.584 --> 00:18:29.324
Send it before you turn
this off, if you can.

00:18:29.564 --> 00:18:34.265
A Tuesday nobody else knows about
is a Tuesday you'll explain away.

00:18:35.086 --> 00:18:36.306
Last pause.

00:18:36.546 --> 00:18:39.026
Write the move in your own words.

00:18:39.327 --> 00:18:42.067
My next move on a Tuesday is.

00:18:42.367 --> 00:18:45.228
Put a day on it. Put a meal on it.

00:18:45.328 --> 00:18:48.109
Put down the name of the man you'll text.

00:18:50.216 --> 00:18:51.056
Good.

00:18:51.216 --> 00:18:53.357
That's a move you can fail at.

00:18:53.517 --> 00:18:56.577
And that's the only kind
that can make a man.

00:18:57.378 --> 00:18:59.478
Let's go over it one more time.

00:18:59.738 --> 00:19:04.199
A man's life gets decided on
the days nobody photographs.

00:19:04.519 --> 00:19:07.180
God builds you in the very little.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.260
Busy is not the same as there.

00:19:10.521 --> 00:19:14.781
And the first mark of a
steadfast man is Stop Waiting.

00:19:14.942 --> 00:19:18.562
The last ordinary day is
the one you answer for.

00:19:18.702 --> 00:19:21.663
The next one is the one you practice on.

00:19:23.083 --> 00:19:27.824
If you trust Christ, you're not trying
to earn your way into anything here.

00:19:27.945 --> 00:19:30.545
Your Father has already claimed you.

00:19:30.725 --> 00:19:34.586
You put the childish ways down
because you belong to Him.

00:19:34.666 --> 00:19:36.266
Not so He'll take you.

00:19:36.386 --> 00:19:39.907
And if you're not sure about Him yet,
you're still welcome here.

00:19:40.027 --> 00:19:42.428
Start with one honest day.

00:19:42.568 --> 00:19:45.248
He's never been afraid of an honest man.

00:19:46.049 --> 00:19:48.209
Look at the word you wrote in the margin.

00:19:48.409 --> 00:19:52.410
That's where your Tuesday goes missing.
Go show up for it.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:56.611
Next lesson we look at
why that's been so hard.

00:19:56.691 --> 00:20:00.512
Why a good man keeps waiting,
even when he knows better.

00:20:00.692 --> 00:20:03.212
You said you were just
going to check this out.

00:20:03.373 --> 00:20:06.393
You stayed. That was your first yes.

00:20:06.533 --> 00:20:07.753
Don't waste it.

00:20:07.874 --> 00:20:09.634
I'll see you in the next lesson.
